  "source": {
    "attribution": "Generated locally from pinned PinMAME and the user-authorized ROM corpus; ROM bytes remain external. Public switch writes are host stimuli, never ROM observations. The runner can checkpoint only segment-display text, so the DMD service-menu navigation is counted pulses, guarded by output checkpoints on 19; every retained DMD frame was visually checked, and each diagnostic snapshot's interpreted_text is that reading of its pixel SHA-256. PinMAME's built-in mechanisms were disabled, so Ted's mouth switch (11) never answered the motor. Exact external directory manifest rs_l6/manifest.json SHA-256 d8e512951bff2b744054816b4749e1c8639377b020816396854cbb00509e6aec (built by tools/build_external_evidence_manifest.py); it lists the raw trace, the copied scenario, the DMD frames and the isolated mutable state, with no ROM bytes.",
